From: CapCut-on-Wine project
Subject: advapi32/sechost: place EnumServicesStatusEx strings at the end of the caller's buffer

SYMPTOM
  A CapCut 9.5.0.4050 run that has already rendered its home screen dies at
  t ~= 98-130 s with, from the crashpad dump:

      EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION (0xc0000005), ExceptionAddress 0x6fffc3619943
      = metasecml.dll + 0x29943

  metasecml.dll is CapCut's VMProtect-packed security/telemetry module, so the
  instruction cannot be read from disk -- but crashpad stores memory around the
  faulting RIP and the whole thread context, so it can be disassembled straight
  out of the dump:

      6fffc3619935: mov  %rax,%r8
      6fffc3619940: inc  %r8
      6fffc3619943: cmpb $0x0,(%rdx,%r8,1)      <-- fault
      6fffc3619948: jne  0x6fffc3619940

  i.e. an inline strlen() of the C string at RDX.  The faulting context is
  RDX = 0x676f6c746e657645 ("Eventlog" -- the *characters* of a service name)
  and R8 = 0, so the "pointer" is the service-name text itself.  Walking the
  faulting thread's stack back (RET at rsp+0x1b8 = metasecml+0x265fa) and the
  +relay log of the same thread identifies the function: it is the one that
  calls OpenSCManagerA and then EnumServicesStatusExA twice (relay lines
  ret=6fffc36197da / 6fffc3619868 / 6fffc36198e2), and the buffer it passes is
  exactly the object the faulting loop walks (the faulting R14 equals the
  relay-logged buffer argument).

ANALYSIS
  That function enumerates the services with

      OpenSCManagerA( NULL, NULL, SC_MANAGER_ENUMERATE_SERVICE )
      EnumServicesStatusExA( scm, SC_ENUM_PROCESS_INFO, SERVICE_WIN32,
                             SERVICE_ACTIVE, NULL, 0, &needed, &returned, ... )
      EnumServicesStatusExA( scm, ..., buffer, needed, ... )

  and then walks the returned array of ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA with a
  0x38 stride until an entry's lpServiceName or lpDisplayName is NULL:

      if (!e->lpServiceName || !e->lpDisplayName) break;
      push_back( std::string(e->lpServiceName) );

  Windows anchors the strings at the END of the caller's buffer and zeroes the
  space between the array of structures and that string block, so the entry
  right after the last returned service is { NULL, NULL, ... } and the walk
  stops.  Wine packed the strings immediately after the array, so
  entry[returned] was the first service name -- a non-NULL "pointer" holding
  the characters "Eventlog" -- and the strlen() dereferenced it.

MEASURED (identical calls on the Windows 11 guest and in Wine; the probes are
work/tools/svcenum_probe.c and svcenumw_probe.c, buffer pre-filled with 0xAA so
every byte the API writes is visible)

  EnumServicesStatusExA, SERVICE_WIN32/SERVICE_ACTIVE, size == needed

  | observation                           | Wine before         | Wine after          | Windows 11          |
  |---------------------------------------|---------------------|---------------------|---------------------|
  | entry[returned].lpServiceName         | 0x676f6c746e657645  | 0000000000000000    | 0000000000000000    |
  |                                       | ("Eventlog")        |                     |                     |
  | string block (byte offsets in buffer) | [280 .. 412]        | [836 .. 968]        | [6596 .. 12912]     |
  |                                       | right after array   | buffer end (968)    | buffer end (12920)  |
  | zeroed bytes between array and strings| 0                   | 556                 | 1724                |
  | buffer size == 'needed'               | 968                 | 968                 | 12920 (87 services) |

  The Windows string offsets shift by exactly the change in buffer size (+512 and
  +8192 were measured), i.e. Windows anchors the block to the end of the buffer;
  Wine after the patch does the same.  Windows also zeroes the whole gap: the
  probe pre-filled the buffer with 0xAA and every byte between the array and the
  strings came back zero.

  EnumServicesStatusExW behaves the same way on Windows (strings end exactly at
  `size`, gap zeroed, entry[returned] zero); Wine packed them after the array.

CLASSIFICATION
  GENERAL WINE GAP FOUND WHILE MAKING CAPCUT RUN, NOT A CAPCUT-EXCLUSIVE HACK.
  The buffer layout is part of the API contract ("an array of
  ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESS structures, followed by the strings"), Windows
  really does anchor the string block to the end of the caller's buffer and zero
  the space after the array, and any caller that stops iterating on a NULL entry
  misbehaves on Wine for every input.  The patch therefore lives in the shared
  series, not in patches/local/.

CHANGE
  * dlls/sechost/service.c, EnumServicesStatusExW(): after the "does it fit"
    check, compute the string-block offset as size - string_bytes instead of
    count * sizeof(entry), and zero the space between the array and the strings
    before copying them.
  * dlls/advapi32/service.c, EnumServicesStatusExA(): same layout for the ANSI
    strings (a pre-pass measures the ANSI string bytes with
    WideCharToMultiByte(..., NULL, 0) so the block can be anchored at the end),
    plus a proper ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER when the caller's buffer cannot hold
    array + strings (the old code underflowed `n` and could write past the
    buffer).
  * dlls/advapi32/tests/service.c: test_enum_svc_ex() now also runs both the A
    and the W call into a deliberately oversized buffer and asserts the whole
    layout -- the entry right after the last returned service must be NULL, the
    space up to the string block must be zeroed, and the string block must be
    anchored at the end of the buffer.  Without the fix that is 6 failures
    (three per call: no gap, no NULL entry, block not anchored); with it,
    769 tests executed / 0 failures.

  The non-Ex EnumServicesStatusW/A wrappers lay their own strings out from the
  start; they were not measured against Windows and are not touched here.

diff --git a/dlls/advapi32/service.c b/dlls/advapi32/service.c
index bcf92d7..53d4c46 100644
--- a/dlls/advapi32/service.c
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/service.c
@@ -293,7 +293,7 @@ EnumServicesStatusExA( SC_HANDLE hmngr, SC_ENUM_TYPE level, DWORD type, DWORD st
     ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA *services = (ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA *)buffer;
     ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSW *servicesW = NULL;
     WCHAR *groupW = NULL;
-    DWORD sz, n;
+    DWORD sz, n, total;
     char *p;
 
     TRACE("%p %u 0x%lx 0x%lx %p %lu %p %p %p %s\n", hmngr, level, type, state, buffer,
@@ -321,7 +321,24 @@ EnumServicesStatusExA( SC_HANDLE hmngr, SC_ENUM_TYPE level, DWORD type, DWORD st
                                  needed, returned, resume_handle, groupW );
     if (!ret) goto done;
 
-    p = (char *)services + *returned * sizeof(ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA);
+    /* Windows anchors the strings at the end of the caller's buffer and zeroes
+     * the space right after the array of structures, so that a caller which
+     * walks the array until a NULL entry stops there. */
+    for (i = 0, total = 0; i < *returned; i++)
+    {
+        total += WideCharToMultiByte( CP_ACP, 0, servicesW[i].lpServiceName, -1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL );
+        if (servicesW[i].lpDisplayName)
+            total += WideCharToMultiByte( CP_ACP, 0, servicesW[i].lpDisplayName, -1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL );
+    }
+    if (*returned * sizeof(ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA) >= size ||
+        total > size - *returned * sizeof(ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA))
+    {
+        SetLastError( ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER );
+        goto done;
+    }
+    p = (char *)services + size - total;
+    memset( (char *)services + *returned * sizeof(ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA), 0,
+            (p - (char *)services) - *returned * sizeof(ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA) );
     n = size - (p - (char *)services);
     ret = FALSE;
     for (i = 0; i < *returned; i++)
diff --git a/dlls/advapi32/tests/service.c b/dlls/advapi32/tests/service.c
index 33ff25d..2db74f7 100644
--- a/dlls/advapi32/tests/service.c
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/tests/service.c
@@ -1545,6 +1545,29 @@ retry:
     return alldone;
 }
 
+/* Windows anchors the enumerated service strings at the end of the caller's
+ * buffer and zeroes the space between the array of structures and the strings.
+ * A caller that walks the array until a NULL entry (as CapCut's metasecml.dll
+ * does) therefore stops right after the last service; Wine used to pack the
+ * strings immediately after the array, so that walk ran into the strings.
+ * strstart/strend are the first byte and the end of the string block. */
+static void check_enum_services_layout( const BYTE *buf, DWORD size, DWORD returned,
+                                        DWORD entry_size, DWORD strstart, DWORD strend )
+{
+    DWORD arrend = returned * entry_size, i;
+
+    ok( strstart > arrend, "expected a gap between the array of structures and the strings\n" );
+    ok( arrend + entry_size <= size, "no room for a NULL entry after the array\n" );
+    ok( *(const void **)(buf + arrend) == NULL,
+        "expected a NULL entry right after the last returned service\n" );
+    for (i = arrend; i < strstart; i++)
+        if (buf[i]) break;
+    ok( i == strstart, "expected the space after the array to be zeroed, byte %lu is %#x\n",
+        i, buf[i] );
+    ok( size - strend <= entry_size, "expected the strings anchored at the end of the buffer, "
+        "%lu of %lu bytes left over\n", size - strend, size );
+}
+
 static BOOL test_enum_svc_ex(int attempt)
 {
     SC_HANDLE scm_handle;
@@ -1553,8 +1576,10 @@ static BOOL test_enum_svc_ex(int attempt)
     DWORD neededA, returnedA;
     DWORD tempneeded, tempreturned, missing;
     DWORD servicecountactive, servicecountinactive;
+    DWORD strstart, strend;
     ENUM_SERVICE_STATUSW *services;
     ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSW *exservices;
+    ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA *aservices;
     UINT i;
 
     /* More or less the same for EnumServicesStatusExA */
@@ -1776,6 +1801,89 @@ static BOOL test_enum_svc_ex(int attempt)
     /* Store the number of returned services */
     tempreturned = returned;
 
+    /* Windows anchors the enumerated strings at the end of the caller's buffer
+     * and zeroes the space between the array of structures and the strings, so
+     * a caller that walks the array until a NULL entry (CapCut's metasecml.dll
+     * does exactly this) stops right after the last service.  A deliberately
+     * oversized buffer makes both the anchor and the zeroed gap non-trivial.
+     * This is checked for the A call CapCut uses and for the W call; Wine used
+     * to pack the strings right after the array, so entry[returned] held the
+     * first service name and the walk ran into it. */
+    exservices = malloc(tempneeded + 0x2000);
+    bufsize = tempneeded + 0x2000;
+    needed = 0xdeadbeef;
+    returned = 0xdeadbeef;
+    SetLastError(0xdeadbeef);
+    ret = pEnumServicesStatusExW(scm_handle, 0, SERVICE_WIN32, SERVICE_STATE_ALL,
+                                 (BYTE *)exservices, bufsize, &needed, &returned, NULL, NULL);
+    if (ret)
+    {
+        strstart = ~0u; strend = 0;
+        for (i = 0; i < returned; i++)
+        {
+            DWORD o;
+            if (exservices[i].lpServiceName)
+            {
+                o = (BYTE *)exservices[i].lpServiceName - (BYTE *)exservices;
+                if (o < strstart) strstart = o;
+                o += (lstrlenW(exservices[i].lpServiceName) + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR);
+                if (o > strend) strend = o;
+            }
+            if (exservices[i].lpDisplayName)
+            {
+                o = (BYTE *)exservices[i].lpDisplayName - (BYTE *)exservices;
+                if (o < strstart) strstart = o;
+                o += (lstrlenW(exservices[i].lpDisplayName) + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR);
+                if (o > strend) strend = o;
+            }
+        }
+        check_enum_services_layout( (BYTE *)exservices, bufsize, returned,
+                                    sizeof(ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSW), strstart, strend );
+    }
+    free(exservices);
+    if (!ret && GetLastError() == ERROR_MORE_DATA && attempt)
+        goto retry; /* service start race condition */
+    ok(ret, "Expected success, got error %lu\n", GetLastError());
+    ok(needed == 0, "Expected needed buffer to be 0 as we are done\n");
+    ok(returned == tempreturned, "Expected the same number of service from this function\n");
+
+    aservices = malloc(tempneeded + 0x2000);
+    bufsize = tempneeded + 0x2000;
+    needed = 0xdeadbeef;
+    returned = 0xdeadbeef;
+    SetLastError(0xdeadbeef);
+    ret = pEnumServicesStatusExA(scm_handle, 0, SERVICE_WIN32, SERVICE_STATE_ALL,
+                                 (BYTE *)aservices, bufsize, &needed, &returned, NULL, NULL);
+    if (ret)
+    {
+        strstart = ~0u; strend = 0;
+        for (i = 0; i < returned; i++)
+        {
+            DWORD o;
+            if (aservices[i].lpServiceName)
+            {
+                o = (BYTE *)aservices[i].lpServiceName - (BYTE *)aservices;
+                if (o < strstart) strstart = o;
+                o += strlen(aservices[i].lpServiceName) + 1;
+                if (o > strend) strend = o;
+            }
+            if (aservices[i].lpDisplayName)
+            {
+                o = (BYTE *)aservices[i].lpDisplayName - (BYTE *)aservices;
+                if (o < strstart) strstart = o;
+                o += strlen(aservices[i].lpDisplayName) + 1;
+                if (o > strend) strend = o;
+            }
+        }
+        check_enum_services_layout( (BYTE *)aservices, bufsize, returned,
+                                    sizeof(ENUM_SERVICE_STATUS_PROCESSA), strstart, strend );
+    }
+    free(aservices);
+    if (!ret && GetLastError() == ERROR_MORE_DATA && attempt)
+        goto retry; /* service start race condition */
+    ok(ret, "Expected success, got error %lu\n", GetLastError());
+    ok(needed == 0, "Expected needed buffer to be 0 as we are done\n");
+
     /* Allocate less than the needed bytes and don't specify a resume handle.
